& [IR7ResourceSafetyHumanApprovalAndRollbackContractV1] is the IR7-S03 contract for resource safety, human approval, credential, network, and rollback semantics
  + [contract_id] is ir7-resource-safety-human-approval-and-rollback-contract-v1
  + [contract_uuid] is e2cea44e-e912-4640-b7c9-d560b393903c
  + [slice_id] is IR7-S03
  + [source_chunk] is IR7 operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [authority_scope] is resource target safety classification, risk escalation, blast radius, credential boundary, network boundary, rollback and abort route, monitoring route, human approval freshness, expiration, revocation, refusal, and escalation routing
  + [implementation_scope] is safety contract only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: define resource-safety semantics that future dry-run simulations can use without granting live-control permission
  = must: preserve that human approval records are explicit, fresh, scoped, revocable planning inputs rather than blanket live-control authority
  = must: classify unknown, ambiguous, credential-touching, network-touching, destructive, process, GPU, model-runtime, and job-queue targets as high-risk or critical until reviewed
  = must: require completion review before IR7-S04 fixture planning opens
  - never: grant broad approval authorization, execute live operations, access credentials, mutate network exposure, perform destructive filesystem actions, create fixture files, create expected ledgers, create generated outputs, install dependencies, mutate package metadata, dispatch agents, authorize operations control, or authorize live machine control in this slice

